metro police say they've arrested the  man responsible for two violent crimes  that happened last week a murder  and a separate shooting police say both  crimes happened in the area of decatur  and penwood  just south of sahara orcomanna reports  police say a homeless man was shot and  killed in this area last monday  and then just days later another man was  shot but he survived  now police say that they found the  person responsible  21 year old nola green was arrested in  connection to both crimes police have  surveillance video from july 13  showing the homeless man identified as  48-year-old brent lloyd  being shot to death and the shooter is  said to be green a couple days later a  man was shot in the chest while walking  his dog police say both shootings seemed  similar and were unprovoked  a tip led police to green and they found  disturbing videos on green's cell phone  showing both shootings including the  homeless man's murder  police calling it a thrill killing we  are confident in saying  today that we believe we have taken a  very  dangerous person off of the streets  and we believe that he would have  committed the crime of murder again  had it not been for the actions of this  agency  police are also continuing to look at  more evidence to figure out if green is  connected  to any other violent crimes in the area  green faces murder  and attempted murder charges he's being  held without bail  and is due in court wednesday reporting  in las vegas orca mana 8 news now
 

